WEBVTT

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.354
"On the night of the third
anniversary of Funtom's founding,

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.691
they'll be presenting a free
play for orphaned children.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.986
The show will be Hamlet."

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:30.947
I see we're getting a fair bit of press.

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:33.825
I didn't anticipate you
doing charity work like this.

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:37.078
I admire your philanthropic spirit,
young master.

00:00:37.078 --> 00:00:39.164
Philanthropic?

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:43.585
These days love breeds money.

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:47.088
People will say
"Funtom gives orphaned children love."

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:49.716
We can use that to our advantage--

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:56.765
Love for the poor orphans!
Oh, it brings tears to my eyes!

00:00:56.765 --> 00:01:02.771
Our young master must know how
they feel because he lost his own father!

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:08.985
Are you lot even listening to me?!

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:14.616
Just what I'd expect from our
young master-- or rather, from a <i>child.</i>

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.871
Hamlet, hmm?

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.877
After Prince Hamlet's father,
the king, is murdered,

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:29.339
Hamlet vows to avenge him
even at the cost of his own life.

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:34.260
The play might as well have
been written for you, young master.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.931
It just happened to be in the
repertoire of the troupe I hired.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.766
I don't care about the plo--

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.309
Y-Young master!

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:43.311
What? An accident?

00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:47.732
Yes, my lord. The ship carrying
the actors ran into some trouble,

00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:51.736
and they won't arrive in
London until next week, no!

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.657
The show is in three days!

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:58.451
Do you know how much advertising I've done?!

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.204
The press will be all over us that day.

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:03.623
We can't possibly reschedule.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.502
What shall we do, my lord?

00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:11.381
We have no choice.

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:13.758
Sebastian, this is an order:

00:02:13.758 --> 00:02:19.264
Make the show a success-- make it
worthy of the Phantomhive name.

00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:21.266
Yes, my lord.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.071
"Black Butler"

00:02:35.071 --> 00:02:41.453
<i>Since then, I've actually</i>
<i>come to like the night somewhat</i>

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:46.833
<i>In a sea of dependence,</i>
<i>I forget even to breathe</i>

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:50.295
<i>When I'm right on the verge</i>
<i>of losing my head over you</i>

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:54.049
<i>You just leave me lukewarm</i>

00:02:54.049 --> 00:03:01.556
<i>The aesthetic of leave-taking</i>
<i>despises a self-satisfied kiss</i>

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:07.479
<i>Don't leave me alone, show me</i>
<i>compassion, paint me with death</i>

00:03:07.479 --> 00:03:14.319
<i>In your room, all words slip away</i>

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:20.241
<i>I want to end like this, cloaked</i>

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:27.123
<i>But the night ignores</i>
<i>that wish and brings morning</i>

00:03:27.123 --> 00:03:33.880
<i>With your gentle,</i>
<i>passionate, and dastardly kiss</i>

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.133
<i>Paint this final night</i>

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:41.554
<i>The moon illuminates us</i>

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.532
Well, Ran-Mao, what part do you want to play?

00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:02.158
Seaweed.

00:04:02.158 --> 00:04:06.287
If I'm going to be in a play,
naturally I'll be Ramakrishna!

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:10.125
Oh, Prince Soma, I just know you'll be sublime!

00:04:10.125 --> 00:04:17.340
I want to be a princess! And wear
a poofy skirt with three petticoats!

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:22.429
If we're going all-out,
perhaps I should put on four or five.

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:25.223
What? You, a princess?

00:04:25.223 --> 00:04:27.726
That wouldn't be cute at all!

00:04:27.726 --> 00:04:31.813
Seaweed, an Indian, and two princesses?

00:04:31.813 --> 00:04:34.524
I told you, this is Hamlet!

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:39.904
Sebastian! Why all these amateurs?
Are you putting on a school play?!

00:04:39.904 --> 00:04:43.033
In its proper form, a charity play

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:46.411
is something staged at home
by the master of the house.

00:04:46.411 --> 00:04:50.331
It's not something you pay
a theatrical troupe to do.

00:04:50.331 --> 00:04:54.961
Moreover, I believe this particular group...

00:04:54.961 --> 00:05:01.968
...will tolerate a bit of harsh direction.

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:06.973
Naturally, you'll be
performing as well, young master.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:13.980
I'm sure you understand what
the best response is to this crisis.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.983
After all, you're an <i>adult</i>, aren't you?

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:23.073
"Vocal Exercises"

00:05:25.283 --> 00:05:27.911
It's time to begin.

00:05:27.911 --> 00:05:30.747
We'll start with vocal exercises.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.763
No hanky-panky.

00:05:47.764 --> 00:05:48.973
Go!

00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:55.730
Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.273
No curry.

00:05:57.273 --> 00:05:58.692
It's very good.

00:05:58.692 --> 00:06:01.403
There's plenty to go around, if you'd like--

00:06:01.403 --> 00:06:02.821
No, thank you.

00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:06.825
Next, performance training.

00:06:06.825 --> 00:06:09.828
"Performance Training"

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:16.167
"To be, or not to be: that is the question."

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:19.879
Young master, put more heart into it.

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:24.050
--That's a <i>dead </i>certainty! Not to be, of course!☆
--"T-To be, or not to be--"

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.677
--That's a <i>dead </i>certainty! Not to be, of course!☆

00:06:29.556 --> 00:06:32.559
What pathetically dull acting!

00:06:32.559 --> 00:06:36.563
Do us all a favor and drop dead
this instant, you hideous Hamlet!

00:06:36.563 --> 00:06:38.857
Grell! What are you doing here?

00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:43.153
Who's that? I have the strangest
feeling I've seen him before...

00:06:43.153 --> 00:06:46.448
You have no heart. No heart!

00:06:46.448 --> 00:06:49.409
You're not conveying
Hamlet's tortured anguish!

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:52.078
You have to make it echo through the theater!

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:54.289
Come on, do it like <i>this</i>.

00:06:55.331 --> 00:07:01.212
"To be, or not to be: that is the question."

00:07:01.212 --> 00:07:02.672
No!

00:07:02.672 --> 00:07:08.053
♪ That's no question at all! ♪

00:07:08.053 --> 00:07:10.388
♪ Not at all! ♪

00:07:10.388 --> 00:07:14.351
♪ When I met you, it changed me! ♪

00:07:14.351 --> 00:07:18.188
♪ The important thing <i>is lo</i>ve! ♪

00:07:20.982 --> 00:07:25.695
No, I unquestionably recommend death to you.

00:07:25.695 --> 00:07:29.366
I see that love stands always
but a step away from death!

00:07:29.366 --> 00:07:32.786
Oh, Sebas-<i>chan</i>, my excitement increases!

00:07:35.622 --> 00:07:40.001
Still, this melodramatic, dubious acting...

00:07:40.001 --> 00:07:44.214
It may be worth making use of
for a limited period of time.

00:07:44.214 --> 00:07:47.634
At any rate, none of you have
a sufficient sense of urgency.

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:49.469
Put more into this.

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.137
I told you, no curry!

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:52.847
It's very good.

00:07:52.847 --> 00:07:54.391
Seaweed.

00:07:54.391 --> 00:07:55.975
Here.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:08:00.355
See? Pink hats really are the best kind!

00:08:00.355 --> 00:08:01.773
Sebastian?

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:09.197
Hamlet.

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:13.243
The lack of even the faintest
ray of hope in its plot

00:08:13.243 --> 00:08:17.622
prompts people to group it with
Othello, King Lear, and Macbeth

00:08:17.622 --> 00:08:22.168
as one of Shakespeare's
four greatest tragedies.

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:25.630
In order for you to
truly understand Hamlet,

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:33.263
I'll first give you a taste
of the Phantomhive tragedy.

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:41.980
S-Sebas-<i>chan</i>, how terrifying you are!

00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:19.893
Oh, look, the viscount!

00:09:26.066 --> 00:09:28.651
The house is packed!

00:09:28.651 --> 00:09:31.488
Woo-hoo! Now I'm gettin' worked up!

00:09:35.909 --> 00:09:40.580
Ah, now I'm really
showing my stuff as an actress.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:45.001
Ugh, this costume isn't cute at all!

00:09:48.171 --> 00:09:49.464
Where is the young master?

00:09:49.464 --> 00:09:53.093
E-Er, I think he went to the W.C., yes...

00:09:57.263 --> 00:10:01.726
So here you are.

00:10:01.726 --> 00:10:06.439
It's a bit too late to say you
don't like the part, young master.

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:11.820
A young prince who loses his
father and burns for revenge...

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:16.950
You deliberately gave me this part.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.160
Not only do you have no acting experience,

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:24.666
you also lack the dexterity
to button your own shirts.

00:10:24.666 --> 00:10:27.585
I felt casting you in a part
too different from yourself

00:10:27.585 --> 00:10:29.879
would be hard on you, my lord.

00:10:29.879 --> 00:10:30.880
What?!

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.300
What's the harm in it?

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:38.304
Let's make this a prelude to
the bloody revenge coming.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:45.812
Young master, are you all ready?

00:10:45.812 --> 00:10:49.816
The curtain is finally
rising on this tale of revenge.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:09.336
<i>An adult's holiday.</i>

00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:17.260
<i>Pluto knows there are certain tastes</i>
<i>only a connoisseur can appreciate.</i>

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.931
Crunchy and bracing!

00:11:21.931 --> 00:11:25.143
Headlong doggie!

00:11:25.143 --> 00:11:27.354
<i>Inukko: a Funtom Company product.</i>

00:11:33.276 --> 00:11:35.695
The previous king of Denmark has died,

00:11:35.695 --> 00:11:42.369
and his younger brother
Claudius has been crowned king!

00:11:42.369 --> 00:11:47.165
The late king's wife, whom
he'd loved unconditionally,

00:11:47.165 --> 00:11:52.379
has become the bride of the new ruler!

00:11:52.379 --> 00:11:56.716
Oh, I'm ever so sad that my brother died,

00:11:56.716 --> 00:12:01.262
but since <i>we're </i>still alive,
we must enjoy ourselves!

00:12:01.262 --> 00:12:03.473
I quite agree.

00:12:03.473 --> 00:12:05.850
Slip...

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:11.981
Oh, you're perfect! Such stiff ribs!

00:12:11.981 --> 00:12:18.029
Tickle, tickle, tickle...

00:12:18.029 --> 00:12:23.159
I know I said I wanted laughter,
but a direct attack like this is cheating!

00:12:23.159 --> 00:12:26.788
Tickle, tickle, tickle!

00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:37.090
The late king's son Hamlet
encounters him as a ghost!

00:12:38.383 --> 00:12:45.015
O Father, what may this mean,
that thou appearest before me so?

00:12:47.225 --> 00:12:50.311
I see, my vile uncle Claudius

00:12:50.311 --> 00:12:56.526
hath killed thee by pouring poison in thy ear?

00:12:58.695 --> 00:13:00.947
Yes, I see.

00:13:00.947 --> 00:13:03.992
Thou bid'st me take revenge in thy place.

00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:09.289
But of course, Father!

00:13:09.289 --> 00:13:11.291
He can understand that?

00:13:11.291 --> 00:13:14.794
Tanaka is a magnificent actor who
can convey it all with his aura, yes!

00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:19.507
More importantly, why am I a stagehand?!
I don't accept this!

00:13:19.507 --> 00:13:21.801
It's because you're eating curry.

00:13:21.801 --> 00:13:30.268
Father... Thy hatred hath
survived the very fires of hell.

00:13:30.268 --> 00:13:35.273
Here and now I swear I shall avenge you!

00:13:36.775 --> 00:13:39.486
What an enthusiastic performance!

00:13:39.486 --> 00:13:42.072
Damn it, man, move that
light further to the right!

00:13:42.072 --> 00:13:45.116
I ask you, why am I a stagehand?!

00:13:45.116 --> 00:13:47.660
I tell you, because you're eating curry.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.497
Now, how is the audience reacting?

00:13:56.127 --> 00:14:00.090
It seems Hamlet is too
difficult for children to understand.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:03.093
In order to deceive his uncle,

00:14:03.093 --> 00:14:07.305
Hamlet pretends to be
disappointed in his love for Ophelia,

00:14:07.305 --> 00:14:10.308
the daughter of the king's
chief counsel, and go mad!

00:14:12.352 --> 00:14:19.359
Ah, what a sinful woman I am!

00:14:19.359 --> 00:14:21.736
Ophelia, there you are!

00:14:21.736 --> 00:14:26.783
Father! Hmm, now that
I get a better look at thee,

00:14:26.783 --> 00:14:28.368
I see thou art quite handsome!

00:14:28.368 --> 00:14:34.290
Never mind that Hamlet, I fancy <i>you</i>, Father!

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:38.294
Such a honeyed scent
doth forbidden love have!

00:14:42.007 --> 00:14:43.341
What depravity!

00:14:43.341 --> 00:14:48.346
Only Brahmā could be forgiven
such acts between father and daughter!

00:14:50.056 --> 00:14:51.933
But...

00:14:51.933 --> 00:14:55.854
What with one thing
and another, Ophelia died!

00:14:55.854 --> 00:15:01.401
No! It's not Ophelia's death scene... yet...

00:15:01.401 --> 00:15:04.529
Agents who die in the field receive no burial!

00:15:04.529 --> 00:15:07.949
Let's toss her in the river!

00:15:11.536 --> 00:15:14.330
Father...

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:24.799
--♪ Seaweed. Oh how I love it... ♪

00:15:24.799 --> 00:15:27.635
--Goodness, she seems to be a hit.
--♪ Seaweed. Oh how I love it... ♪

00:15:27.635 --> 00:15:28.970
--Seaweed!
--♪ Seaweed. Oh how I love it... ♪

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.765
--Hey, it's seaweed!
--♪ Seaweed. Oh how I love it... ♪

00:15:31.765 --> 00:15:35.226
It sounds like she's popular
with the tadpoles, yes.

00:15:35.226 --> 00:15:38.688
I don't get kids.

00:15:38.688 --> 00:15:44.694
Now that the ice is broken, the young
master's big scene is here at last.

00:15:47.364 --> 00:15:50.116
To be, or not to be:

00:15:50.116 --> 00:15:53.161
That is the question.

00:15:53.161 --> 00:15:59.042
My uncle is a cunning man.

00:15:59.042 --> 00:16:04.881
Even if I'm able to carry out my revenge,
I shan't escape alive.

00:16:04.881 --> 00:16:09.302
And... the truth is...

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:14.182
<i>I don't want </i>to die.

00:16:18.395 --> 00:16:21.731
Quit being a coward, Hamlet!

00:16:21.731 --> 00:16:27.153
Drive out that foolish,
stunted soul of thine this instant!

00:16:28.321 --> 00:16:31.950
My vow is a bloody one.

00:16:34.244 --> 00:16:37.455
There's no turning back now!

00:16:44.212 --> 00:16:49.217
Now let me be off, before the
blazing sun in my blood rises.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:54.431
Hey!

00:16:54.431 --> 00:16:58.059
The young master is amazing!

00:16:58.059 --> 00:17:01.271
Yes, very true-to-life.

00:17:06.609 --> 00:17:09.738
Oh, that fury that makes
his slender limbs tremble!

00:17:09.738 --> 00:17:14.659
That burning rage is like an aloof ruby!

00:17:14.659 --> 00:17:18.371
Oh, dear. Pardon me.

00:17:18.371 --> 00:17:23.376
Well, well. That performance
resonated even with the children.

00:17:23.376 --> 00:17:25.003
Now, then...

00:17:26.296 --> 00:17:28.131
I'm on.

00:17:29.257 --> 00:17:34.471
Hamlet and Ophelia's brother
Laertes must cross blades

00:17:34.471 --> 00:17:38.475
in a fencing match arranged by the king!

00:17:47.067 --> 00:17:50.111
But the tip of Laertes's sword
is coated with a poison

00:17:50.111 --> 00:17:54.324
that will kill a man after just
the faintest scratch of his blade!

00:17:57.619 --> 00:17:59.996
I-I'm scared...

00:17:59.996 --> 00:18:02.999
Thou art Ophelia's brother, then?

00:18:02.999 --> 00:18:05.460
I have heard thy skill is great!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:10.298
I have heard the same of thine.
I hope thou shalt go easy on me.

00:18:11.466 --> 00:18:17.597
Now, I think that's enough chat!
We'll have a ten-point match.

00:18:17.597 --> 00:18:21.393
And now... let the match be--

00:18:21.393 --> 00:18:24.145
Hamlet, no!

00:18:24.145 --> 00:18:28.608
That old guy's sword is poisoned!

00:18:28.608 --> 00:18:29.943
"Old guy"?

00:18:29.943 --> 00:18:33.071
Yeah, they lied when they
said this was a fencing match!

00:18:33.071 --> 00:18:35.865
They're trying to kill you, Hamlet!

00:18:35.865 --> 00:18:39.369
You should stop! You should
stop trying to get revenge, okay?

00:18:39.369 --> 00:18:40.954
I don't want any stupid revenge!

00:18:40.954 --> 00:18:43.915
Don't die, Hamlet!

00:18:43.915 --> 00:18:45.834
"Don't die"...

00:18:45.834 --> 00:18:49.671
Young master! Your line, your line!

00:18:49.671 --> 00:18:51.297
My line?

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:56.761
Oh, it's hopeless!

00:18:56.761 --> 00:18:57.971
You there! Draw the curtains!

00:18:57.971 --> 00:19:00.807
R-Right, yes! Er...

00:19:00.807 --> 00:19:03.101
No, wait.

00:19:03.101 --> 00:19:05.311
How dare thee let thy eyes wander?

00:19:12.777 --> 00:19:16.906
The farce is over. I'll tell thee the truth.

00:19:16.906 --> 00:19:21.745
My beloved sister's sweet life was ended

00:19:21.745 --> 00:19:24.122
because of her involvement with thee!

00:19:24.122 --> 00:19:26.541
Wait! This isn't in the script!

00:19:26.541 --> 00:19:30.920
I shall win my revenge by slaying thee!

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:33.173
My beloved Ophelia...

00:19:33.173 --> 00:19:35.925
♪ Stop the fighting! ♪

00:19:35.925 --> 00:19:40.555
♪ Don't you fight over me! ♪

00:19:40.555 --> 00:19:41.765
What the devil is he doing?!

00:19:41.765 --> 00:19:43.641
When did he get a gondola?!

00:19:43.641 --> 00:19:45.643
It's not fair to take the
spotlight all for yourself!

00:19:45.643 --> 00:19:47.145
I'm going to go out there and--

00:19:47.145 --> 00:19:49.064
Wait! If you go out there now--

00:19:49.064 --> 00:19:50.732
Not fair! Not fair!

00:19:50.732 --> 00:19:54.778
Ophelia?! I thought you were dead!

00:19:54.778 --> 00:19:57.322
When my dear brother's
love rained down upon me,

00:19:57.322 --> 00:20:02.160
the flower of life bloomed
anew with deadly haste!☆

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:06.998
Oh, dear brother! You are truly the one for--

00:20:11.544 --> 00:20:13.171
Ouchies!

00:20:14.839 --> 00:20:18.176
So <i>this </i>is where you've been dallying,

00:20:18.176 --> 00:20:19.761
Grell Sutcliff.

00:20:19.761 --> 00:20:21.012
Will!

00:20:21.012 --> 00:20:24.182
This is an outrage.
Not only have you deserted your post,

00:20:24.182 --> 00:20:27.352
you're actually putting on a
charity play with a loathsome demon.

00:20:27.352 --> 00:20:31.564
Ah, now three men are fighting over me!

00:20:31.564 --> 00:20:34.693
Stop, stop, stop! No fighting!

00:20:34.693 --> 00:20:39.823
You just leave everything to me,
Ramakrishna, avatar of the sun!

00:20:39.823 --> 00:20:41.408
Prince Soma!

00:20:41.408 --> 00:20:43.159
Ophelia came back to life!

00:20:43.159 --> 00:20:45.161
Go get him, Rama-whatsit!

00:20:48.581 --> 00:20:51.960
This is a mess! What a foolish--

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:54.462
Yes, it is foolish.

00:20:54.462 --> 00:20:56.673
Revenge is foolish.

00:20:56.673 --> 00:21:01.136
All it offers is confusion
and a brief fever of excitement.

00:21:01.136 --> 00:21:07.642
When the curtains close on
this pipe dream, nothing is left.

00:21:07.642 --> 00:21:10.562
Isn't that right, my lord Hamlet?

00:21:10.562 --> 00:21:13.857
Seba-- I mean, I never
thought I'd hear you say...

00:21:13.857 --> 00:21:15.692
Quite so!

00:21:15.692 --> 00:21:18.528
Revenge is utterly meaningless!

00:21:18.528 --> 00:21:22.824
Ramakrishna, avatar of the sun, guarantees it!

00:21:22.824 --> 00:21:24.409
H-Hey!

00:21:24.409 --> 00:21:29.622
A demon's master who
can't ad-lib isn't worth his salt.

00:21:31.958 --> 00:21:33.585
Hamlet...

00:21:36.296 --> 00:21:37.714
That's right.

00:21:41.509 --> 00:21:45.764
I'll forget about revenge and live on!

00:21:45.764 --> 00:21:48.600
I will live as long as Nature allows me to!

00:21:56.358 --> 00:21:58.401
Magnificent!

00:21:58.401 --> 00:22:03.740
This is the true Hamlet which
transcends a mere revenge play!

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:07.327
I long to wrap this pitiable yet dignified
Hamlet in the bacon of my arms!

00:22:07.327 --> 00:22:10.955
Ham, ham-ham, I'll be your eggs, Ham...!

00:22:22.342 --> 00:22:23.968
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:22:25.095 --> 00:22:34.270
<i>All the world's a stage, and all</i>
<i>the men and women merely players.</i>

00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:38.650
<i>We meet and begin our drama.</i>

00:22:38.650 --> 00:22:43.196
<i>And sooner or later, the curtain closes.</i>

00:22:43.196 --> 00:22:48.076
<i>Thank you. Thank you.</i>

00:22:48.076 --> 00:22:50.704
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:23:10.265 --> 00:23:17.480
<i>The moonlight that reveals</i>
<i>sorrow was coldly illuminating</i>

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:27.282
<i>The despair and the future</i>
<i>which grew intimate in the dark</i>

00:23:27.282 --> 00:23:34.831
<i>With the secret you gave me as my guide</i>

00:23:34.831 --> 00:23:41.546
<i>I move through the blue night's stillness</i>

00:23:41.546 --> 00:23:48.428
<i>Lacrimosa, I want to love once again</i>

00:23:48.428 --> 00:23:56.102
<i>The dazzling world that</i>
<i>crumbled and vanished in the distance</i>

00:23:56.102 --> 00:24:03.276
<i>I'll hide my dreams within my eyes</i>

00:24:03.276 --> 00:24:21.294
<i>Until the tears fall on my sullied heart</i>

00:24:26.508 --> 00:24:28.009
That was fun!

00:24:28.009 --> 00:24:30.428
Hamlet was so dashing!

00:24:34.265 --> 00:24:37.394
A smashing performance, and it
was all thanks to you, Ran-Mao!

00:24:37.394 --> 00:24:38.603
Seaweed.

00:24:38.603 --> 00:24:41.064
Hmm? Where'd Ophelia go?

00:24:41.064 --> 00:24:43.149
That chap with the side part
took her off somewhere.

00:24:43.149 --> 00:24:45.777
Beat her black and blue first, too!

00:24:51.032 --> 00:24:56.204
You seem out of sorts for someone
whose Hamlet was such a success.

00:24:56.204 --> 00:25:00.834
I'll have you know I don't
seriously intend to forget revenge.

00:25:00.834 --> 00:25:02.669
I know, my lord.

00:25:03.670 --> 00:25:07.424
In the end, stories enacted on the
stage are naught but pipe dreams.

00:25:07.424 --> 00:25:10.093
And after all, it would be
quite an inconvenience for me

00:25:10.093 --> 00:25:13.013
if you were to forget about revenge.

00:25:13.013 --> 00:25:16.016
Ciel!

00:25:17.350 --> 00:25:20.311
Now we're going to celebrate
with a party at your manor!

00:25:20.311 --> 00:25:22.313
What? But...

00:25:22.313 --> 00:25:24.399
I made a trip home during the intermission

00:25:24.399 --> 00:25:27.485
and prepared all the ingredients for the feast.

00:25:27.485 --> 00:25:30.697
You see, I am merely one hell of a butler.

00:25:37.829 --> 00:25:43.835
<i>I'll forget about revenge and live on...</i>

00:25:50.508 --> 00:25:52.510
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:54.429 --> 00:25:56.431
"Tanaka Sushi"

00:25:56.890 --> 00:25:59.100
Hang in there, Papa!

00:26:00.060 --> 00:26:04.230
Sorry, but I'm a fishmonger,
not a gossipmonger.

00:26:04.230 --> 00:26:07.317
Why don't you get the hell out of my town?

00:26:07.317 --> 00:26:11.529
It's only a matter of time
before Tanaka Sushi goes under.

00:26:11.529 --> 00:26:13.907
What, you've brought in outside talent?

00:26:13.907 --> 00:26:15.658
"Nutrition Education"
How amusing.

00:26:15.658 --> 00:26:17.660
"Nutrition Education"
Let's see what he's got.

00:26:17.660 --> 00:26:20.789
Take this! Freshly caught and still floppin'!

00:26:20.789 --> 00:26:23.416
What I roll are human hearts.

00:26:25.001 --> 00:26:27.212
Say your prayers, Tanaka lackey!

00:26:29.047 --> 00:26:30.674
Mr. Bastian...

00:26:31.257 --> 00:26:36.680
"Tanaka Sushi"

00:26:39.891 --> 00:26:43.353
"New Series: Black Sushi Chef"

00:26:43.353 --> 00:26:45.355
Perhaps black fingernails are a no-no after all?

00:26:45.355 --> 00:26:49.234
"Look forward to it!"
